        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                   MAUS: KEY FACTS                                |\n|                                                                  |\n|  CREATOR: Art Spiegelman (b. 1948, Stockholm; grew up NYC)       |\n|  SERIALIZATION: RAW Magazine, 1980-1991                          |\n|  PUBLISHED: Vol 1 (1986, Pantheon); Vol 2 (1991, Pantheon)       |\n|  AWARD: Pulitzer Prize Special Citation (1992)                   |\n|         First (and for years only) comic to win a Pulitzer       |\n|                                                                  |\n|  SUBJECT: Vladek Spiegelman's Holocaust survival (Auschwitz)     |\n|           AND: Art interviewing his elderly father in the 1970s  |\n|           DUAL NARRATIVE: past and present simultaneously        |\n|                                                                  |\n|  DEVICE: Ethnic groups as animals                                |\n|           Jews = mice; Nazis = cats; Poles = pigs                |\n|           Americans = dogs; French = frogs                       |\n|                                                                  |\n|  STRUCTURE: A comic about Holocaust AND about making a comic     |\n|             about the Holocaust                                  |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
